  "summary": "Proposal for the generic-runtime-objects slice of the engine. The dominant cluster is replay/game-state IO: ReplayDataFileWriter (0x004B7500) records a full 104-slot replay to a file or performs a one-shot buffer-chain dump, QueuePop (0x004B7A00) drains the same node list into window accumulators, SaveHotlapData (0x004B7DE0) writes .HOT lap files, and ReplayFileLoadStateMachine (0x004BA1F0) drives the VCR playback loader. These share a file/stream backend (0x00566xxx) and a string-table message interface (0x00423A00 + byte_5EC4C0/byte_5EC4CC). A second cluster is generic intrusive linked-list removal (0x004BA830, 0x004BACF0, 0x004BB0C0) operating on 12-byte nodes, plus the dual-list allocator AllocDualListBlockAndInsertNodes (0x004BAFC0). Support pieces include AngleClampWrap (0x004B86E0), serialization magic detection (0x004B8090), a loading state-transition gate (0x004B8AE0) that ticks many global subsystems, a key-priority multi-path dispatcher (0x004BA180), and a replay-status UI renderer (0x004B9FD0). Ownership is established for only ReplayPlaybackLoaderStateMachine and DualListContainer (DERIVED, from packet owners); most owners stay UnknownObject, and equal byte offsets on different bases (0xF30/0xF34/0xF38/0xF3C/0xF80 appear on several independent objects) are deliberately not merged.",
